<TITLE>Motorcycle ride from Coeur d'Alene Idaho back home 2022-09-10</TITLE>
<meta name="msvalidate.01" content="5EDDD546C69B870E0A70F093CCAF7A59" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
</HEAD>
<BODY bgcolor="#ffffff">
<H2>Motorcycle ride along the Columbia River starting from Priest Lake ID, riding the International Selkirk Scenic Loop and ending up in Coeur d'Alene Idaho 2022-09-09</H2>
<a href="https://www.google.com/maps/d/u/0/viewer?mid=1nNlAtZPZLR6cF9LKx3c138Lz__yaugA" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09.jpg"  ALIGN=RIGHT style="width:350px"></A>
<BR><BR>
<BR><BR>
The <A HREF="https://www.npr.org/programs/invisibilia/" target="_blank">Invisibilia podcast</A> discussed <A HREF="https://www.wabe.org/invisibilia-the-great-narrative-escape-slow-tv/" target="_blank">Norwegian 'Slow TV'</A>. I decided to make this entire trip all <A HREF="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slow_television" target="_blank">Slow TV</A> videos. This <a href="https://youtu.be/RosO_9AQbKc" target="_blank">video is the ride</A> for the entire day.
<BR><BR>
Starting at <A HREF="https://visitnorthidaho.com/community/priest-lake-idaho/" target="_blank">Priest Lake</A> at the <a href="https://www.elkinsresort.com/" target="_blank">Elkins Resort</A> I travveld back south to meet up again with the Selkirk Scenic loop. Nice day except for the smoke from the fires. Got gas when I arrived on Route 2, continued on Route 2 for a little bit to Route 20 and headed north. Nice ride <A HREF="https://www4.bing.com/maps?cp=48.86621~-117.361786&lvl=17.950296&dir=304.96008&style=x" target="_blank">in the mountains</A>:
<BR>
<A HREF="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_01_route_20.jpg" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_01_route_20.jpg" style="width:900px"></A><BR><BR>
And arrived at the Metaline Falls / Nelway Border Crossing. Here you see both the US side and the Canadian side:
<BR><A HREF="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_02_us_canada_border.jpg" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_02_us_canada_border.jpg" style="width:900px"></A>
<BR><BR>
As you head north on Highway 6 / 3 and as you ride in the mountains you meet up with the <A HREF="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kootenay_River" target="_blank">Kootenay River</A> in the city of Nelson, you <A HREF="https://www4.bing.com/maps?cp=49.52946~-117.26651&lvl=15.7&style=h" target="_blank">follow the river</A> and the Kootenay Lake for the rest of the ride in Canada:
<BR>
<A HREF="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XOcBedf0WKl91bvwqdz9XPXi7YNZIsu5/view?usp=share_link" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_03_kootenay_sm.jpg"></A>
<BR><BR>
Rode down to the ferry crossing at <A HREF="https://www4.bing.com/maps?cp=49.62438~-116.95957&lvl=17&style=h" target="_blank">Balfour</A>, Rode across the lake to Pilot bay. Again, a free ferry:
<BR>
<BR><A HREF="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_04_kootenay_lake_ferry.jpg" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_04_kootenay_lake_ferry.jpg" style="width:900px"></A>
<BR><BR>
From there it was a turn back south riding all along the <A HREF="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kootenay_Lake" target="_blank">Kootenay Lake</A>:
<BR>
<BR><A HREF="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_05_kootenay_lake.jpg" target="_blank"><IMG SRC="Motorcycle/motorcycle_columbia_selkirk_2022-09-09_05_kootenay_lake.jpg" style="width:900px"></A>
<BR><BR>
From there crossed the border back into the United states and south to Coeur d'Alene. Ready to get home the next day.
<BR><BR>
